# DERIVED ART - never commit it.
#
# `.paxmesh` is BAKED for a location: it stores its texture paths as length-prefixed
# strings (`ships/<root>_diffuse`), so a mesh baked in one folder looks for its textures
# relative to where it was baked, not to where it ends up. Committing one means shipping a
# mesh that points at somebody else's disk. It has to be rebuilt where the art is placed.
#
# The siblings below are generated from the same source `.obj` for the same reason.
*.paxmesh
*.pointcube
*.rawbitmap
*1024.png
*256.png

# Build output
__pycache__/
*.tmp
mast.compile.log
mast.runtime.log

# ---- Art-pipeline working set -------------------------------------------------
#
# Everything here is REGENERABLE from `new/races/` plus the scripts in `_tools/`, and
# together it is ~2.1 GB - an order of magnitude more than the mod itself. The two
# .safetensors are also 218 MB EACH, over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, so a push
# containing them is rejected outright rather than merely slow.
#
# What is NOT ignored, deliberately: `new/races/` (the Gemini source sheets - those came
# from a generator and cannot be reproduced) and `media/` (the built, shipped art).
_tools/out/
_tools/lora_out/
_tools/lora_data/

# Staging for the face work - intermediate crops, spikes and Blender scratch.
new/gen/
new/work/
new/builder/

# The standalone site from `sbs site --emit site` - build output, not source.
__site__/
